<title>SPAIN: Spain Oct CPI rose 0.1 pct, yr/yr 3.5 pct. [Corrected 11:52 gmt]</title>
<headline>Spain Oct CPI rose 0.1 pct, yr/yr 3.5 pct. [Corrected 11:52 gmt]</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Statistics Institute (INE) gave the following figures:</p>
<p> SPANISH INFLATION		OCT 96    SEPT 96  OCT 95</p>
<p> Monthly CPI index change     0.1	   0.2	 0.2</p>
<p> Year-on-year rise		3.5	   3.6	 4.3</p>
<p> Core inflation		   0.2	   0.2	 0.4</p>
<p> Year-on-year rise		3.2	   3.4	 4.9</p>
<p> INDEX BY COMPONENTS	     OCT 96    SEPT 96     YR/YR</p>
<p> Food				 -0.3	   0.2	  3.8</p>
<p> Clothing			    0.5	   0.2	  2.5</p>
<p> Housing			     0.7	   0.4	  4.4</p>
<p> Household goods		   0.1	   0.2	  4.0</p>
<p> Medicine			    0.2	   0.1	  3.6</p>
<p> Transport			   0.3	   0.1	  3.2</p>
<p> Culture			     0.6	   0.7	  2.8</p>
<p> Other				-0.1	   0.2	  3.5</p>
<p>NOTE- In food, fresh food declined 0.8 percent from the previous month (3.9 percent year-on-year) and processed food was unchanged (3.7 percent year-on-year). (Corrects erroneously swapped categories)</p>
</text>
